Subject: [PATCH 6.1.y 0/2] can: isotp: backport of 2 patches that failed to
 apply to 6.1-stable

This resubmits "can: isotp: fix use-after-free race with concurrent
NETDEV_UNREGISTER" (commit 20bab8b88baac140ca3701116e1d486c7f51e311
upstream), which failed to apply to the 6.1-stable tree, together
with "can: isotp: serialize TX state transitions under so->rx_lock"
(commit cf070fe33bfbd1a4c21236078fadb35dd223a157 upstream) from the
same upstream series, which builds on it and would otherwise fail
for the same reason. This is the full set of 3 upstream isotp.c
patches from 7.2-rc3 minus the 1 already queued by the normal stable
process for 6.1 ("can: isotp: use unconditional synchronize_rcu()
in isotp_release()").

Same scope as linux-5.15.y: 6.1-stable already carries the
sk_error_report() wrapper throughout isotp.c, so isotp_tx_timeout()
applies unmodified. isotp_init() still needs adaptation for the same
two independent, not-backported prerequisites: the dynamic
max_pdu_size TX buffer resize (commits 2f2dd39 "can: isotp: set max
PDU size to 64 kByte", 2022, and 973bb01 "can: isotp: add module
parameter for maximum pdu size", 2023, neither Cc: stable) and the
hrtimer_setup() API consolidation. The corresponding hunks are
omitted or adapted to the older code shape; the actual race fixes
themselves are unaffected and fully applied. See each patch's
changelog for the exact adaptation.

This assumes the 1 already-queued isotp.c patch for 6.1-stable has
landed by the time this is applied. If not, please let me know and I
will rebase.

Oliver Hartkopp (2):
  can: isotp: fix use-after-free race with concurrent NETDEV_UNREGISTER
  can: isotp: serialize TX state transitions under so->rx_lock

